# Secrets — never commit real credentials.
#
# `.env` must be matched at EVERY depth, not just demo/: .env.example tells the
# reader to copy it to either the module root or demo/, and a root-only or
# demo-only pattern silently leaves the other one committable. The negation
# re-includes the templates, which are generated and carry no real values.
.env
*.env
# Also .env.local, .env.staging, and anything else suffixed after .env —
# these hold real values too. Negations come last so they win.
.env.*
!*.env.example
!.env.example

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# Go build output.
# `go build ./...` in a main package drops an executable named after its
# directory, with no extension — *.exe and *.test do not catch it.
*.exe
*.test
*.out
/demo/demo

*.log

# The generator's per-model markdown is superseded by pkg.go.dev now that
# openapi/ is a public package, so it stays out of the repo — and therefore out
# of the module zip, which Go builds from the VCS tree.
#
# docs/* rather than docs/: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY
# is excluded, so excluding the contents is what makes the negation below work.
docs/*
# API.md and apis/ are ours, not the generator's, and carry the one thing
# pkg.go.dev cannot: which HTTP endpoint each method calls, with its parameters.
# Re-including the directory is enough — `docs/*` matches only direct children,
# so nothing excludes the files inside it.
!docs/API.md
!docs/apis/
